For duplicate-key detection: 
```python
node = yaml.compose(text, Loader=yaml.SafeLoader)
def walk(node, path, out):
    if isinstance(node, yaml.MappingNode):
        seen = {}
        for k_node, v_node in node.value:
            key = k_node.value if isinstance(k_node, yaml.ScalarNode) else repr(k_node)
            line = k_node.start_mark.line + 1
            if key in seen:
                out.append({"key": key, "lines": [seen[key], line], "path": path})
            else:
                seen[key] = line
            walk(v_node, path + "." + str(key), out)
```
Note: duplicate keys in PyYAML's compose don't raise; safe_load silently last-wins.

Scalar collection: walk node tree, yield scalar values with path.

